@base = http://localhost:5194
# After `dotnet run --project Backend/MiniBank.Api` (Development, `http` profile in launchSettings.json):
# Scalar UI: {{base}}/scalar  |  OpenAPI: {{base}}/openapi/v1.json
# Demo users (seeded): demo@minibank.local / Demo123!  and  sara@minibank.local / Demo123!
@token = YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN
@accountId = YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID

### Health (always mapped)
GET {{base}}/health
Accept: application/json

### OpenAPI document (all environments)
GET {{base}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

### Register a new customer (anonymous, replaces disabled /register)
POST {{base}}/customers/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new.user@test.com",
  "password": "Demo123!",
  "fullName": "New User",
  "phoneNumber": "09123456789"
}

### Login (Identity API, bearer token)
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@minibank.local",
  "password": "Demo123!"
}

### My profile (identity from token — no id needed)
GET {{base}}/customers/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### My overview — one page: full name, email, phone + every account number with balance + total balance (USD)
GET {{base}}/customers/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Update my profile
PUT {{base}}/customers/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "New Name",
  "phoneNumber": "09123456789"
}

### My KYC status
GET {{base}}/kyc/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Submit my KYC (only the document id — customer is the caller)
POST {{base}}/kyc/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "primaryDocumentId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### My documents
GET {{base}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### My risk info
GET {{base}}/risk/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### My accounts with balances
GET {{base}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Statement (paged)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/statement?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Deposit (idempotent — reuse key returns same tx; different amount => 409)
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 100,
  "idempotencyKey": "demo-deposit-manual-1"
}

### Fake-gateway top-up — body is ONLY the USD amount (no card, no key; always approves valid amounts)
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/topup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 100
}

### My transactions across all my accounts (newest first, paged; balances via /accounts)
GET {{base}}/transactions/mine?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Withdraw
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 50,
  "idempotencyKey": "demo-withdraw-manual-1"
}

### Preview transfer destination (full + masked holder name, no balances)
POST {{base}}/transfers/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "toAccountId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### Step 2 of account-number flow: enter IR-XXXXXXXXXX or 16-digit number → see holder's FULL name before confirming (USD amount entered in step 1)
POST {{base}}/transfers/preview-by-number
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountNumber": "IR-1234567890"
}

### Step 3: confirm + transfer by account number (saveBeneficiary = remember checkbox for next transfers)
POST {{base}}/transfers/by-account-number
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "toAccountNumber": "IR-1234567890",
  "amount": 25,
  "saveBeneficiary": true
}

### Saved beneficiaries (remembered account number + holder name for next transfers)
GET {{base}}/beneficiaries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Save a beneficiary manually (nickname optional display name)
POST {{base}}/beneficiaries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountNumber": "IR-1234567890",
  "nickname": null
}

### Transfer (source must be owned by caller)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "toAccountId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "amount": 25,
  "idempotencyKey": "demo-transfer-manual-1"
}
